//
// PROBE: the collecting mode, set inside a body the tier compiles (RFC-0005
// criterion 18). Each word opens with `1 2 + drop`, which gives its body a
// site, so that at `--jit-threshold 1` it is compiled on its first call and
// entered compiled on the next two. What follows `:` must be collected as
// the reference collects it:
//   a literal or a CALL is appended into the value beneath
//     (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/multistackvm_apply.rs:19-27,
//      reference/rust_multistackvm/src/multistackvm_apply.rs:89-97);
//   a CONTEXT is pushed as a value of its own
//     (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/multistackvm_apply.rs:72-73);
//   and onto a value that is not a container, "appended" is replaced
//     (reference/rust_dynamic/src/push.rs:162-168).
// `bang` sets the mode by a computed name, through `!`.
//
:lit { 1 2 + drop : 7 ; } register
[ 0 ] lit lit lit
:called { 1 2 + drop : 7 nl ; } register
[ 0 ] called called called
:ctx { 1 2 + drop : 7 @side ; } register
[ 0 ] ctx ctx ctx
:bang { 1 2 + drop ":" ! 7 nl ; } register
[ 0 ] bang bang bang
:scalar { 1 2 + drop : 7 ; } register
5 scalar scalar scalar
